# Cloudflare Pages headers file — applied at the edge for every route.
#
# next.config.js already defines an equivalent `headers()` block, but it is
# NOT actually applied in production: this project deploys via
# @cloudflare/next-on-pages, and Next's headers() config does not carry
# through that adapter onto Cloudflare Pages (verified — curl against the
# live site showed none of these headers present despite the config
# existing in code, the same class of bug as the /prices static-cache issue
# documented in NEW_PAGE_SPEC.md). This file is the actual source of truth
# for response headers on this deployment.
#
# Intentionally NOT included here: a strict Content-Security-Policy. A CSP
# tight enough to matter can silently break Stripe Checkout, Google
# Analytics/Tag Manager, or the Supabase client if the allowlist is wrong —
# that risk isn't worth taking without dedicated testing of every
# third-party integration first.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-DNS-Prefetch-Control: on
  Referrer-Policy: origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups
